IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cea-types`
IMPORT `cea-dates`

-- Customs and Excise Act 2018 — GOALS 2 AND 3: DUTY, ITS PAYMENT, AND LATE
-- PAYMENT PENALTIES.
--
--   "How much duty, by when must it be paid, and what penalty has accrued
--    if it is late?"
--
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/act_public_2018_4.txt — ss 120,
-- 122-124, 159-160.

§ `Goal 2 — duty and its payment`

-- s 120 "When duties are imposed according to a specified quantity, weight,
-- size, or value, the duties must be charged proportionately on a greater or
-- smaller quantity, weight, size, or value." The rates are in the Tariff.
@ref s 120
GIVEN valueRate IS A NUMBER, value IS A NUMBER, unitRate IS A NUMBER, quantity IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the duty at` valueRate `of a value of` value `and` unitRate `on each of` quantity `units` MEANS
    valueRate TIMES value PLUS unitRate TIMES quantity

-- s 122 "the duty on imported goods must be paid to Customs when— (a) the
-- goods have been entered ... and the entry has been passed for home
-- consumption; or (b) ... entered ... for removal to a manufacturing area; or
-- (c) ... wrongfully landed ...; or (d) an offence ... has been committed".
-- s 123(1): a deferred time for an authorised person. s 124 "(2) Duty that
-- results from an amendment of an assessment under section 112 must be paid
-- ... within 20 working days after the date on which the assessment is
-- amended. (3) ... an assessment under section 113 ... within 20 working days
-- after the date on which written notice of the assessment is given ... (4)
-- ... sections 114 to 116 ... (5) ... section 117 ... (6) Duty that is
-- demanded under section 138(3) or 139(4) must be paid ... within 20 working
-- days after the date on which the demand is given. (7) [the chief executive
-- may] require the person to pay the duty within an earlier time specified in
-- the notice" (s 124(7) added after the independent pass).
@ref ss 122-124
@export The last day for paying duty under ss 122-124 of the Customs and Excise Act 2018 (NZ): the day of the s 122 event (or the deferred date under an s 123 authorisation); otherwise the 20th working day after an amended assessment, a Customs assessment or notice, or a demand. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN d IS A `Duty facts`  @desc The occasion for payment and its date, and any deferred date
      matariki IS A LIST OF DATE  @desc The Matariki Observance Days
GIVETH A DATE
`the payment date for` d `, Matariki days` matariki MEANS
    CONSIDER d's `payment occasion`
    WHEN `s 122 on entry or other event` THEN
        CONSIDER d's `deferred payment date under s 123`
        WHEN JUST deferred THEN deferred
        WHEN NOTHING THEN d's `occasion date`
    WHEN `s 124(7) an earlier time required by notice` THEN d's `occasion date`
    OTHERWISE `the` 20 `th working day after` (d's `occasion date`) `, Matariki days` matariki

§ `Goal 3 — late payment penalties`

-- s 160 "(3) Section 159 applies to any duty in respect of imported goods if
-- section 123(1) applies to the payment of the duty. ... (5) Section 159
-- applies to any duty if the duty is required to be paid within a period
-- given by section 124(2) to (7)." (1)-(2): excise duty under Schedule 3
-- cl 5(a), not in scope.
@ref s 160(3)-(6)
GIVEN d IS A `Duty facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 159 applies to` d IF
    CONSIDER d's `payment occasion`
    WHEN `s 122 on entry or other event` THEN
        CONSIDER d's `deferred payment date under s 123`
        WHEN JUST deferred THEN TRUE
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- The duty still to be paid at the close of a day.
GIVEN duty IS A NUMBER, d IS A `Duty facts`, x IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the duty of` duty `still unpaid under` d `at the close of` x MEANS
    max 0 (duty MINUS sum (map (GIVEN p YIELD p's `amount paid`) (filter (GIVEN p YIELD p's `paid on` AT MOST x) (d's `payments made`))))

-- s 159 "(1) A penalty is payable ... if— (a) section 160 provides for this
-- section to apply to the duty; and (b) the duty is not fully paid to Customs
-- before the close of the payment date ... (2) The penalty is equal to 1% of
-- the amount of the duty still to be paid ... as at the close of the payment
-- date. (3) A further penalty is payable ... if the duty is not fully paid ...
-- before the close of the seventh day after the payment date. (4) The further
-- penalty is equal to 4% of the amount of the duty still to be paid ... as at
-- the close of that seventh day." Each penalty is counted once the close of
-- its day falls on or before the day of measurement (fork F2).
@ref ss 159, 160
@export The late payment penalties on duty under ss 159-160 of the Customs and Excise Act 2018 (NZ), where they apply (deferred duty under s 123 and duty payable within 20 working days under s 124): 1% of the duty unpaid at the close of the payment date, and a further 4% of the duty unpaid at the close of the 7th day after it, counting payments made by then. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN duty IS A NUMBER  @desc The duty payable
      d IS A `Duty facts`  @desc The occasion and its date, any deferred date, and the payments made
      matariki IS A LIST OF DATE  @desc The Matariki Observance Days
      asAt IS A DATE  @desc The day at whose end the penalties are measured
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the late payment penalties on duty of` duty `, facts` d `, Matariki days` matariki `, as at` asAt MEANS
    IF   NOT `section 159 applies to` d
    THEN 0
    ELSE first PLUS further
    WHERE
        due MEANS `the payment date for` d `, Matariki days` matariki
        seventh MEANS `the day` 7 `days after` due
        first MEANS IF due AT MOST asAt THEN 0.01 TIMES `the duty of` duty `still unpaid under` d `at the close of` due ELSE 0
        further MEANS IF seventh AT MOST asAt THEN 0.04 TIMES `the duty of` duty `still unpaid under` d `at the close of` seventh ELSE 0
